# Wave W17-AC (Route 228): wash thorn — a cactus-patch thorn tree: a ribbed green column with two arms and a single red crown flower, spine dots along its ribs, standing on wash turf (ground baked in) — the design’s SCARECACT patch standing in the tree register, honest sparse crown (design: the sand country’s green island keeps its cactus patch; the herder’s charges graze around it). Route 228’s own tree — split from every pine in the program by form entire (a thorn column, not a conifer) and from Maris’s desert trees by company: this thorn stands in a patch on walked green, theirs stand alone in dunes.
